<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Is this original research?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">No. It is a digest of published regulator pages and law-firm summaries, each listed in the Sources section with its date. Zunkiree Labs did not run any survey or collect any data for it.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Is there a single global rule on where AI data must be stored?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">None of the sources in this digest describes one. Each market sets its own rules, mostly about accountability and safeguards when personal data is transferred, rather than a blanket ban on processing abroad.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Do any of these markets require data to stay in the country?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">The sources reviewed describe transfer conditions, not a general requirement to keep personal data in-country. Specific sectors or public bodies may have stricter rules that this digest does not cover, so check your sector.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">How current is the information?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Each fact is stated as of its source date, which ranges from 2009 for one Canadian guideline to October 2026 for the EU timeline summaries. Check the current regulator page before relying on any point.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

